From 2dd8867d222885d484867d3b660635d72fa2d984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dov Slansky <dslansky@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:33:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] harness-device: read a reply on the glass and hear it on the
 speaker

For a host without a terminal (agent-dial), two optional welcome features:

- reply.read: a swipe up on an agent's face opens the existing "latest
  result" reader (the summary's `text`, 1 KB) instead of sending a terminal
  scroll. The reader's drag now stops at the end of the text.
- speak: the reader's [listen] sends `speak` {agentId}; the host answers
  speak.begin, 16 kHz mono PCM frames, speak.end, and the dial plays them
  through the ES8311 speaker from a 3 s PSRAM buffer. [stop], leaving the
  reader, or starting the microphone ends it. Notice mute does not apply:
  speech is asked for.

Question text grows from 255 to 1023 bytes (the state lives in PSRAM).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
